config BR2_PACKAGE_PENGY_PONG
	bool "pengy-pong"
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_RUSTC_TARGET_ARCH_SUPPORTS
	select BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_RUSTC
	help
	  Penguin Pong: two paddles on a 60x20 field, one ball, first to
	  eleven (win by two at 10-10, hard cap 15). The PengyOS pack-in game
	  in the Pong slot (next to floe, merge, icefield, breakout, invaders,
	  lander, blocks, solitaire and rogue). Rust, std only, zero
	  dependencies: the recipe is an offline cargo build and the game needs
	  no libraries at run time. Terminal=true, so it runs in any terminal,
	  over ssh, and on Core.

	  w/s (or the arrow keys) move your paddle, 1/2/3 pick the penguin's
	  difficulty, m toggles 1P/2P hotseat, space serves, p pauses, r
	  restarts, q quits. The best result is kept in
	  $XDG_DATA_HOME/pengyos/games/pengy-pong/, under the player's home.

	  --mono draws with plain ASCII when the locale cannot render the box
	  drawing characters.

	  https://github.com/pengyos/tree/main/tools/pengy-pong
